pocket-motion-only: a gradient paint recolours every pixel an op writes by a per-pixel function of its screen position, which the software rasteriser does by wrapping its target; the PSP GE, ESP32 PPA, Symbian GLES2 and Vita GXM backends interpolate vertex colours across triangles and cannot place more than two stops or an angle on a rounded box or a glyph. No upstream backend is taught PAINT_PUSH or PAINT_POP; a stream carrying them stops there.

0019 — gradient paint: multi-stop linear gradients at any angle, radial
gradients, and gradient text (`bg-clip-text`). Angle, stop colours and
stop positions are keyframe-animatable. A literal that uses only
`bg-gradient-to-* from-* to-*` compiles and draws exactly as before.

What the patch adds, by file:

- `contracts/spec/spec.ts`, `gen-rust.ts`, `engine/core/src/spec.rs`
  (regenerated): props `gradKind` (170), `gradAngle` (171),
  `gradFromPos`/`gradToPos` (172, 173), `gradVia1..4` and their positions
  (174-181), `bgClip` (182); eleven animatable (bits 47-57); enums
  `GradKind` {Legacy, Linear, Radial} and `BgClip` {Border, Text};
  `DRAW_OP.paintPush = 69`, `paintPop = 70`; `PAINT_MAX_STOPS = 6`.
- `framework/compiler/tailwind.ts`: `via-<color>`, `from-N%`/`via-N%`/
  `to-N%` stop positions, `bg-linear-N`, `bg-linear-[Ndeg]`,
  `bg-linear-to-t|r|b|l`, `bg-radial`, `bg-clip-text|border`, and
  arbitrary `bg-[linear-gradient(...)]` / `bg-[radial-gradient(...)]` with
  up to six `#hex` or palette stops and CSS's position fix-up. A literal
  that needs the paint gets `gradKind`, and a `bg-gradient-to-*`
  direction becomes its angle.
- `framework/compiler/animation.ts`: keyframe properties `gradFrom`,
  `gradTo`, `gradAngle`, `gradFromPos`, `gradToPos`, `gradVia1..4`,
  `gradVia1Pos..4Pos` (`gradFrom`/`gradTo` were animatable and had no
  keyframe name).
- `engine/core/src/style.rs`: the fields; the angle defaults to 180 (to
  bottom), positions to 0 and 1, via positions to NaN (no stop).
- `engine/core/src/draw.rs`: `emit_paint_push` inverts the node's world
  affine and writes t as an affine function of the screen point (linear:
  CSS's gradient line through the centre, as long as the box along it;
  radial: the farthest-corner ellipse), with the stops clamped to 0..1 and
  non-decreasing. A node's ground — including the inside of a rounded
  border — is painted white under PAINT_PUSH/PAINT_POP; under
  `bg-clip-text` the box is left unpainted and the glyph run is painted
  instead (a solid ground colour becomes the glyph colour).
- `engine/core/src/raster.rs`: `GradientPaint` bakes the stops into a
  4096-entry table interpolated premultiplied, so a stop fading to
  transparent keeps its colour; `Painted` wraps the target for the span
  and gives each write the table's colour at the pixel centre, its alpha
  times the op's.
- `engine/core/src/damage.rs`: the word counts; a paint's ops share its
  layer rule, so a change inside one or to it is a full redraw.
- `engine/core/src/tests.rs`: six tests — three stops to the right hit
  each stop and nothing else, angle and radial follow the CSS line, a stop
  fading to transparent keeps its colour, `bg-clip-text` paints only the
  glyphs, a changed gradient redraws in full and equals the full render,
  and a legacy two-stop gradient still emits GRAD_RECT.

2026-10-22, rebased onto 66caf4e5. Main added one middle stop of its own
(99af2166): `via-<color>` compiles to `gradVia` (82) and `gradViaPos` (83,
0.5), and the core draws it on the legacy path as two GRAD_RECT boxes split
at the position. A literal must not carry both, so a via waits until the
literal has parsed: under a `bg-gradient-to-*` direction with no other
paint feature — the gradient main draws itself — it is main's
`gradVia`/`gradViaPos` (`via-N%` sets the position, which main's core
honours); in a literal that needs the paint (an angle, radial, a from/to
position, an arbitrary gradient, `bg-clip-text`) it is `gradVia1` and
`gradVia1Pos`. A via alone no longer makes a literal a paint. `Resolved`'s
stop array is `grad_vias`, beside main's `grad_via`. A run under a scale is
drawn as glyph pages (0017), and `bg-clip-text` opens its paint around
them too; `bg_clip_text_paints_scaled_glyph_pages_too` was red before. The
two draw-list walkers main added know PAINT_PUSH (9 + 2n) and PAINT_POP.

